## an5.191
an5.191:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, these five traditional principles of the brahmins are exhibited these days among hounds, but not among brahmins. | T: “Monks, these five ancient brahmanical traditions are now observed among dogs but not among brahmans.
an5.191:1.2 | S: What five? | T: Which five?
an5.191:1.3 | S: In the past brahmins had sex only with brahmin women, not with others. | T: “In the past, brahman males mated only with brahman females and not with non-brahman females.
an5.191:1.4 | S: These days brahmins have sex with both brahmin women and others. | T: At present, brahman males mate with brahman females and with non-brahman females.
an5.191:1.5 | S: But these days hounds have sex only with female hounds, not with other species. | T: At present, male dogs mate only with female dogs and not with female non-dogs.
an5.191:1.6 | S: This is the first ancient principle of the brahmins exhibited these days among hounds, but not among brahmins. | T: This is the first ancient brahmanical tradition that is now observed among dogs but not among brahmans.
an5.191:2.1 | S: In the past brahmins had sex only with brahmin women in the fertile phase of the menstrual cycle, not at other times. | T: “In the past, brahman males mated with brahman females only in-season and not out-of-season.
an5.191:2.2 | S: These days brahmins have sex with brahmin women both in the fertile phase of the menstrual cycle and at other times. | T: At present, brahman males mate with brahman females in-season and out-of-season.
an5.191:2.3 | S: But these days hounds have sex only with female hounds when they are in heat, not at other times. | T: At present, male dogs mate with female dogs only in-season and not out-of-season.
an5.191:2.4 | S: This is the second ancient principle of the brahmins exhibited these days among hounds, but not among brahmins. | T: This is the second ancient brahmanical tradition that is now observed among dogs but not among brahmans.
an5.191:3.1 | S: In the past brahmins neither bought nor sold brahmin women. They lived together because they loved each other and wanted their family line to continue. | T: “In the past, brahman males did not buy or sell brahman females, but took up cohabitation for the sake of reproduction simply through mutual attraction.
an5.191:3.2 | S: These days brahmins both buy and sell brahmin women. They live together whether they love each other or not and they want their family line to continue. | T: At present, brahman males buy and sell brahman females, and take up cohabitation for the sake of reproduction simply through mutual attraction.
an5.191:3.3 | S: But these days hounds neither buy nor sell female hounds. They live together because they’re attracted to each other and want their family line to continue. | T: At present, male dogs do not buy or sell female dogs, but take up cohabitation for the sake of reproduction simply through mutual attraction.
an5.191:3.4 | S: This is the third ancient principle of the brahmins exhibited these days among hounds, but not among brahmins. | T: This is the third ancient brahmanical tradition that is now observed among dogs but not among brahmans.
an5.191:4.1 | S: In the past brahmins did not store up money, grain, silver, or gold. | T: “In the past, brahmans did not make a stash of wealth, grain, silver, or gold.
an5.191:4.2 | S: These days brahmins do store up money, grain, silver, and gold. | T: At present, brahmans make stashes of wealth, grain, silver, & gold.
an5.191:4.3 | S: But these days hounds don’t store up money, grain, silver, or gold. | T: At present, dogs do not make a stash of wealth, grain, silver, or gold.
an5.191:4.4 | S: This is the fourth ancient principle of the brahmins exhibited these days among hounds, but not among brahmins. | T: This is the fourth ancient brahmanical tradition that is now observed among dogs but not among brahmans.
an5.191:5.1 | S: In the past brahmins went looking for almsfood for dinner at dusk, and for breakfast at daybreak. | T: “In the past, brahmans searched for alms for their morning meal in the morning, and for their evening meal in the evening.
